    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-registration limit: creating an owner is now rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** when 100 or more owners already carry today's date as their `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges, following the existing `CityAtCapacityException` pattern:\n\n1. **`DailyRegistrationLimitException`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending date, thrown when the day's cap is hit.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` that maps the new exception to `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429) with a `ProblemDetail` body.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a check (after the existing validations, before persisting) that throws the exception when the limit is reached, plus a `isDailyRegistrationLimitReached(...)` helper and a `DAILY_REGISTRATION_LIMIT = 100` constant. The helper counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the current day.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (creates 100 owners dated today, expects the 101st to be rejected with 429) passes, and the full suite is green.",
